WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.283 --> 00:00:01.500
- Good morning Believe Nation

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.917
today's message is think big.

00:00:05.126 --> 00:00:06.770
Over to you Vince McMahon.

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:08.854
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.854 --> 00:00:11.793
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.793 --> 00:00:14.453
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:14.453 --> 00:00:18.429
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.429 --> 00:00:21.233
- My dad was talking about selling out,

00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:24.679
and that frightened me
because I didn't know

00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:26.679
if I'd be a part or not.

00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:32.356
So I knew there was just some way

00:00:32.356 --> 00:00:34.879
I had to get my hands on this company.

00:00:34.879 --> 00:00:36.199
- [Narrator] In front of his father

00:00:36.199 --> 00:00:38.036
and a group of doubting investors

00:00:38.036 --> 00:00:41.446
Vince works out a series of
convoluted business deals.

00:00:41.446 --> 00:00:42.938
Somehow it works.

00:00:42.938 --> 00:00:46.418
Vince and Linda McMahon now
own Vince Senior's company.

00:00:46.418 --> 00:00:48.281
McMahon's vision is to create

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:51.688
a truly worldwide pro wrestling franchise.

00:00:51.688 --> 00:00:53.810
- I knew my dad wouldn't have
really sold me the business

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:56.060
had he known what I was going to do.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:59.922
And the vision of an
international point of view

00:00:59.922 --> 00:01:01.590
of our business was nothing new.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.978
I wanted to do that from day
one, my dad thought I was nuts.

00:01:04.978 --> 00:01:07.951
And he was right really but
I didn't know I was nuts.

00:01:07.951 --> 00:01:10.979
And then we just went
ahead about doing it.

00:01:10.979 --> 00:01:13.313
- [Narrator] Vince McMahon,
working with his wife Linda,

00:01:13.313 --> 00:01:15.885
begins building a national
and international brand

00:01:15.885 --> 00:01:18.252
for wrestling, the WWF.

00:01:18.252 --> 00:01:20.358
In the process he will nearly decimate

00:01:20.358 --> 00:01:22.299
the existing wrestling establishment

00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:26.718
in a controversial offensive
worthy of a military commander.

00:01:26.718 --> 00:01:29.072
- He bring in his best wrestlers

00:01:29.072 --> 00:01:31.267
into an area he was trying to capture.

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:33.851
He'd buy time and show videotapes

00:01:33.851 --> 00:01:35.652
of their matches last week.

00:01:35.652 --> 00:01:38.142
"And come to the arena,
come to the Colosseum

00:01:38.142 --> 00:01:41.227
"this Saturday you'll see Antonino Rocca"

00:01:41.227 --> 00:01:43.434
or whom soever he was pushing.

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:46.466
And he would take one at a
time, it was a blitzkrieg.

00:01:46.466 --> 00:01:49.776
- My dad would get these
phone calls from his cronies

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.062
who had these little fiefdoms.

00:01:51.062 --> 00:01:53.016
"Hey Vince, what's your kid doing?

00:01:53.016 --> 00:01:54.729
"He's coming into my territory,

00:01:54.729 --> 00:01:56.088
"he's going to wind up dead,

00:01:56.088 --> 00:01:57.703
"I'm going to crush him like a grape.

00:01:57.703 --> 00:02:00.102
"That means I'm going to
have to come to New York."

00:02:00.102 --> 00:02:02.192
My dad was very very concerned.

00:02:02.192 --> 00:02:04.061
And once he saw that we were succeeding

00:02:04.061 --> 00:02:07.957
in head to head competition with them

00:02:07.957 --> 00:02:09.257
my dad

00:02:09.257 --> 00:02:10.090
began to

00:02:10.932 --> 00:02:14.928
think, "Maybe this is
going to work after all."

00:02:14.928 --> 00:02:16.938
- One promoter after another promoter

00:02:16.938 --> 00:02:19.136
after another promoter.

00:02:19.136 --> 00:02:21.265
And they didn't fight back
and they didn't coalesce

00:02:21.265 --> 00:02:24.470
and they didn't come
together, they watched,

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:27.731
and threw up their hands
and ran like the dickens.

00:02:27.731 --> 00:02:31.898
Not knowing he had a, no money,
and b, they could have won

00:02:32.862 --> 00:02:35.922
and held their position, and Vince won.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.430
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:38.882
The question of the day today is

00:02:38.882 --> 00:02:41.847
I want to know what your big vision is.

00:02:41.847 --> 00:02:44.156
When nobody else is around, when you don't

00:02:44.156 --> 00:02:45.776
have any of the
inhibitions, when you think

00:02:45.776 --> 00:02:47.158
you can do big bold things,

00:02:47.158 --> 00:02:48.650
what is that big vision that you

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:50.620
want to accomplish for
yourself, your business?

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:51.987
Leave it in the comments below,

00:02:51.987 --> 00:02:53.664
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:02:53.664 --> 00:02:54.828
I also want to give a quick shout out

00:02:54.828 --> 00:02:57.987
to Michael Wohltmann from
pontevedrafitness.com.

00:02:57.987 --> 00:03:00.041
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:03:00.041 --> 00:03:03.276
Your One Word, it really really
really means a lot to me.

00:03:03.276 --> 00:03:04.635
So thank you guys again for watching,

00:03:04.635 --> 00:03:06.411
I believe in you, I hope you continue

00:03:06.411 --> 00:03:10.155
to believe in yourself and
whatever your one word is.

00:03:10.155 --> 00:03:12.872
Much love and I'll see
ya again tomorrow morning

00:03:12.872 --> 00:03:15.656
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:03:15.656 --> 00:03:18.183
♫ I wake up every morning

00:03:18.183 --> 00:03:21.988
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:03:21.988 --> 00:03:24.016
- Hey believe nation if you
want some more motivation

00:03:24.016 --> 00:03:28.958
on thinking big stay tuned
for some special bonus clips.

00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:31.069
- Some of you all have a habit of dreaming

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:33.417
within your bank account.

00:03:33.417 --> 00:03:35.687
Some of your thoughts
and visions are so big

00:03:35.687 --> 00:03:40.023
and so outlandish and
so powerful and amazing

00:03:40.023 --> 00:03:42.136
you'll end up talking
yourself out of that dream

00:03:42.136 --> 00:03:45.688
from saying, "I can't afford that."

00:03:45.688 --> 00:03:47.657
Well guess what?

00:03:47.657 --> 00:03:50.393
There's a lot of shit I can't afford.

00:03:50.393 --> 00:03:52.816
There's a lot of visions and dreams

00:03:52.816 --> 00:03:54.983
that I still can't afford.

00:03:56.838 --> 00:03:58.921
I've always had this idea

00:03:59.942 --> 00:04:03.942
that one day I'm going to
meet a multi-billionaire.

00:04:05.791 --> 00:04:08.614
And with this multi-billionaire
we're going to

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:11.313
become the best of friends.

00:04:11.313 --> 00:04:13.317
And he's going to say to me,

00:04:13.317 --> 00:04:17.322
"Tyrese, I got all the money in the world

00:04:17.322 --> 00:04:21.072
but I don't have your
visions or your ideas."

00:04:22.259 --> 00:04:23.926
And I'll say to him,

00:04:25.182 --> 00:04:26.876
"I got you.

00:04:26.876 --> 00:04:31.774
"I'm not going to lie to you,
I'm not going to waste your time.

00:04:31.774 --> 00:04:35.941
"I got big visions and ideas,
I can't afford 'em all,

00:04:37.165 --> 00:04:38.445
"but it's not going to stop me

00:04:38.445 --> 00:04:41.612
"from having these visions and ideas."

00:04:42.561 --> 00:04:44.644
I came here to remind you

00:04:45.757 --> 00:04:49.632
that when people laugh
at your visions and ideas

00:04:49.632 --> 00:04:50.812
it's only because they don't have

00:04:50.812 --> 00:04:54.342
their own visions and ideas
around what they're supposed to

00:04:54.342 --> 00:04:57.342
do with their life or their careers.

00:04:59.475 --> 00:05:02.062
People that don't have

00:05:02.062 --> 00:05:02.895
any dreams

00:05:04.301 --> 00:05:05.468
for themselves

00:05:06.363 --> 00:05:09.497
they tend to be dream killers.

00:05:09.497 --> 00:05:13.289
People that don't have their own visions

00:05:13.289 --> 00:05:15.539
they become vision killers.

00:05:17.286 --> 00:05:18.903
They want nothing more than to talk you

00:05:18.903 --> 00:05:20.903
out of your own visions.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:23.853
They don't have dreams for themselves,

00:05:23.853 --> 00:05:26.577
they don't have any
hopes, they're hopeless,

00:05:26.577 --> 00:05:29.210
they're uninspired, unmotivated.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:32.133
They have no dreams, they have nothing

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:34.550
that they're ambitious about.

00:05:35.971 --> 00:05:38.485
But I want to remind you

00:05:38.485 --> 00:05:40.769
to continue to dream

00:05:40.769 --> 00:05:41.936
and dream big.

00:05:44.766 --> 00:05:48.516
I have a habit of dreaming
with my eyes open.

00:05:51.005 --> 00:05:54.338
I get very inspired by the things I see.

00:05:55.846 --> 00:06:00.270
I'm inspired by architecture,
I'm inspired by photography.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:02.103
I'm inspired by ideas,

00:06:03.135 --> 00:06:07.302
I'm inspired by the idea that
someone can have a vision

00:06:10.688 --> 00:06:14.332
and if that vision had
stayed in their mind

00:06:14.332 --> 00:06:17.191
they would have robbed the
world of the opportunity

00:06:17.191 --> 00:06:19.358
to experience that vision.

00:06:21.026 --> 00:06:23.745
I mean think about this,

00:06:23.745 --> 00:06:25.245
as big as this is,

00:06:26.617 --> 00:06:30.459
the fact that it's in
the middle of the street,

00:06:30.459 --> 00:06:34.019
if they had kept this
idea inside their minds

00:06:34.019 --> 00:06:37.600
I wouldn't be here to look at it.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:39.017
Or experience it.

00:06:40.699 --> 00:06:43.358
This is the power of visions

00:06:43.358 --> 00:06:44.191
and ideas,

00:06:45.384 --> 00:06:46.301
right here.

00:06:47.459 --> 00:06:48.626
Do you see it?

00:06:51.691 --> 00:06:55.858
This is the power of not
allowing anyone to laugh at you.

00:06:57.427 --> 00:06:59.360
When you say I want to build something,

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:02.811
a sculpture that can go in
the middle of the street

00:07:02.811 --> 00:07:06.523
and it can be a iconic sculpture
that will last forever.

00:07:06.523 --> 00:07:09.087
Long after I'm dead and gone this could be

00:07:09.087 --> 00:07:11.897
a sculpture that can stand
in the middle of a street,

00:07:11.897 --> 00:07:14.314
here in the streets of Paris.

00:07:17.504 --> 00:07:20.318
And if this person who built this

00:07:20.318 --> 00:07:21.785
would have allowed people to talked him

00:07:21.785 --> 00:07:25.952
out of their dreams and their
visions it wouldn't be here,

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:29.453
for us to see or experience.

00:07:31.513 --> 00:07:32.930
My voice is gone,

00:07:34.562 --> 00:07:37.645
we had a sold out show here in Paris.

00:07:41.437 --> 00:07:43.687
I just wanted to remind you

00:07:45.569 --> 00:07:47.486
to dream and dream big.

00:07:48.525 --> 00:07:53.285
And understand that your family
and friends and loved ones,

00:07:53.285 --> 00:07:56.755
in most cases, boyfriends, girlfriends,

00:07:56.755 --> 00:07:59.698
they will be the first
to try and talk you out

00:07:59.698 --> 00:08:03.091
of your dreams, your visions and ideas

00:08:03.091 --> 00:08:06.091
as to what you're supposed
to do with your life.

00:08:06.091 --> 00:08:08.872
They will say, "Who wants you

00:08:08.872 --> 00:08:11.348
"when you've already
had two or three kids?

00:08:11.348 --> 00:08:13.932
"Who wants you when you've
put on all that weight?

00:08:13.932 --> 00:08:16.327
"Who wants you when
you're looking like this

00:08:16.327 --> 00:08:18.736
"and been through this
and been through that?

00:08:18.736 --> 00:08:20.342
"Nobody's interested in you.

00:08:20.342 --> 00:08:22.000
"Nobody's checking for you.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.968
"They'll laugh at you,
they'll call you names."

00:08:24.968 --> 00:08:28.051
Because they have no dreams,

00:08:28.051 --> 00:08:31.039
they have no hunger for success.

00:08:31.039 --> 00:08:33.679
They don't have an appetite.

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:35.262
They don't want it.

00:08:41.502 --> 00:08:43.085
I want to win so bad,

00:08:44.751 --> 00:08:47.584
my hunger and appetite for success

00:08:48.838 --> 00:08:50.171
is intimidating.

00:08:51.508 --> 00:08:54.569
It scares the shit out of people.

00:08:54.569 --> 00:08:59.263
I come up with new visions
and ideas every single day

00:08:59.263 --> 00:09:03.230
and people around me
say, "Slow down, stop,

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:07.397
"you're doing too much,
you're appetite is too big."

00:09:09.436 --> 00:09:11.103
I can't help myself.

00:09:11.996 --> 00:09:14.924
I want to build, I want to win.

00:09:14.924 --> 00:09:16.424
I'm a billionaire.

00:09:20.179 --> 00:09:21.846
I was a change-aire,

00:09:23.022 --> 00:09:25.070
I was a dollarnaire,

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:28.487
I was a thousandaire, I am a millionaire.

00:09:29.802 --> 00:09:32.606
There's only one step left.

00:09:32.606 --> 00:09:36.338
The billion, I don't
think I'll see a trillion.

00:09:36.338 --> 00:09:38.588
(chuckles)

00:09:40.329 --> 00:09:43.996
But I know I'll see a
billion, I believe it.

00:09:45.137 --> 00:09:47.994
I believe it and there's
no one in the world

00:09:47.994 --> 00:09:50.994
that can talk me out of that feeling.

00:09:54.955 --> 00:09:58.587
Sending my love all the way from Paris.

00:09:58.587 --> 00:10:01.282
If you make it to the end of this video

00:10:01.282 --> 00:10:02.949
I want you to write,

00:10:04.328 --> 00:10:05.840
"Only those that can see

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:09.007
"the invisible can do the impossible."

00:10:10.778 --> 00:10:14.295
You have to be able to
see what doesn't exist

00:10:14.295 --> 00:10:17.182
in order to be able to pull off or achieve

00:10:17.182 --> 00:10:21.239
what, in most people's minds,
seems to be impossible.

00:10:21.239 --> 00:10:24.406
Only those that can see the invisible,

00:10:25.287 --> 00:10:27.917
being able to see what's not there,

00:10:27.917 --> 00:10:30.627
what is your vision, what is your idea,

00:10:30.627 --> 00:10:33.756
what was that God sent dream?

00:10:33.756 --> 00:10:36.414
Only those that can see the invisible

00:10:36.414 --> 00:10:39.331
can do what seems to be impossible.

00:10:44.007 --> 00:10:46.076
You have to be relentless.

00:10:46.076 --> 00:10:48.157
You have to never let off the gas,

00:10:48.157 --> 00:10:50.161
never stop, never quit.

00:10:50.161 --> 00:10:52.592
Never allow anyone to talk you out

00:10:52.592 --> 00:10:56.759
of the dream, the vision, and
ideas that God has sent you.

00:10:59.268 --> 00:11:02.397
- [Narrator] At a compound
in Mountain View, California,

00:11:02.397 --> 00:11:04.410
internet billionaire Naveen Jain

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:06.119
is hatching a plan that could make him

00:11:06.119 --> 00:11:08.602
the world's first trillionaire.

00:11:08.602 --> 00:11:09.852
- [Man] Naveen.

00:11:10.854 --> 00:11:11.803
Good to see you my friend.

00:11:11.803 --> 00:11:12.776
- [Naveen] Good.

00:11:12.776 --> 00:11:15.238
- [Man] So Naveen the team is
working hard as it usually is.

00:11:15.238 --> 00:11:16.821
- [Naveen] Of course.

00:11:16.821 --> 00:11:17.825
- [Man] So we're going to land on the moon

00:11:17.825 --> 00:11:19.586
somewhere around here,

00:11:19.586 --> 00:11:22.355
close to where the Apollo
spacecraft landed at the equator.

00:11:22.355 --> 00:11:23.976
- [Naveen] How did you pick that area?

00:11:23.976 --> 00:11:26.248
- Well it's, first of all
it's on the near side,

00:11:26.248 --> 00:11:28.501
so it's easily accessible from Earth.

00:11:28.501 --> 00:11:30.671
It's an area, the dark
area, are actually regions

00:11:30.671 --> 00:11:33.778
of lava plains, so
they're not mountainous.

00:11:33.778 --> 00:11:35.505
- [Narrator] Not so long
ago it was the Soviet

00:11:35.505 --> 00:11:37.451
and America's superpowers that were locked

00:11:37.451 --> 00:11:39.636
in a race to land on the moon.

00:11:39.636 --> 00:11:42.363
Now it's Bob and Naveen who
are leading the competition

00:11:42.363 --> 00:11:45.457
to mine precious metals from its surface.

00:11:45.457 --> 00:11:49.314
- Are we still on track to
land on the moon by 2015?

00:11:49.314 --> 00:11:50.745
- [Bob] We're still on track Naveen.

00:11:50.745 --> 00:11:52.318
- Initially we thought the mission

00:11:52.318 --> 00:11:55.153
was going to cost us about $100 million.

00:11:55.153 --> 00:11:56.417
Do you think we can bring the cost down

00:11:56.417 --> 00:11:58.221
to say $50 to $60 million now?

00:11:58.221 --> 00:11:59.239
- [Bob] Yeah, even less.

00:11:59.239 --> 00:12:00.178
- Even less?
- I think the first

00:12:00.178 --> 00:12:02.616
mission will be under 50
and subsequent missions

00:12:02.616 --> 00:12:03.949
may be under 40.

00:12:05.845 --> 00:12:08.413
- When would be able to tell your honey

00:12:08.413 --> 00:12:10.663
that, "I want to take you to the moon"?

00:12:10.663 --> 00:12:11.496
- [Bob] 10 years.

00:12:11.496 --> 00:12:12.329
- 10 years?

00:12:12.329 --> 00:12:13.162
- Not only will it be a honeymoon

00:12:13.162 --> 00:12:14.892
but I can take you my honey to the moon

00:12:14.892 --> 00:12:15.803
and I think that'll be the killer.

00:12:15.803 --> 00:12:18.544
- If you can do that that's real business!

00:12:18.544 --> 00:12:20.443
(bright instrumental music)

00:12:20.443 --> 00:12:23.263
If we can go to the moon for $50 million

00:12:23.263 --> 00:12:25.456
and the cost comes down
to 20 and we're able

00:12:25.456 --> 00:12:29.123
to bring back the things
worth $500 billion,

00:12:30.696 --> 00:12:35.113
I don't care what anybody
says that's a great business.

00:12:35.113 --> 00:12:37.409
Somebody is going to
create a trillion dollar

00:12:37.409 --> 00:12:40.992
industry in space and
we sure hope it's us.

00:12:42.246 --> 00:12:44.023
When you tell somebody what you're doing

00:12:44.023 --> 00:12:46.124
and they don't think it's a crazy idea

00:12:46.124 --> 00:12:48.047
then you're thinking too small.

00:12:48.047 --> 00:12:49.483
So when you walk up to a party

00:12:49.483 --> 00:12:50.958
and people say, "What do you do?"

00:12:50.958 --> 00:12:52.644
"Well I mine the moon."

00:12:52.644 --> 00:12:54.041
"Well that's crazy."

00:12:54.041 --> 00:12:55.473
"Well I'm thinking big."

